Hoist the `std::string_view` specialization of `enable_borrowed_range`

When `RANGE_V3_COMBINE_WITH_STD` is defined, `range_fwd.hpp` declares a
partial specialization of `std::ranges::enable_borrowed_range` that is
constrained on `ranges::enable_borrowed_range<T>`. Forming that constraint
instantiates the *primary* template `ranges::enable_borrowed_range` for
whatever `T` is passed, which can happen before `range/access.hpp` has had a
chance to declare its own partial specialization for
`std::basic_string_view`. With GCC 16 that is diagnosed as

  partial specialization of 'ranges::enable_borrowed_range<std::basic_string_view<_CharT, _Traits> >'
  after instantiation of 'ranges::enable_borrowed_range<std::basic_string_view<char> >'

Declaring the `std::basic_string_view` specialization right after the primary
template in `range_fwd.hpp` guarantees it is visible before anything can
instantiate the primary, so the constraint above resolves to the intended
specialization.

This is a local fix; upstream range-v3 has not addressed it yet.
---
 include/range/v3/range/access.hpp | 6 ------
 include/range/v3/range_fwd.hpp   | 7 +++++++
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/range/v3/range/access.hpp b/range/v3/range/access.hpp
--- a/include/range/v3/range/access.hpp
+++ b/include/range/v3/range/access.hpp
@@ -42,11 +42,6 @@

 namespace ranges
 {
-#if defined(__cpp_lib_string_view) && __cpp_lib_string_view >= 201603L
-    template<class CharT, class Traits>
-    RANGES_INLINE_VAR constexpr bool
-        enable_borrowed_range<std::basic_string_view<CharT, Traits>> = true;
-#endif

 // libstdc++'s <span> header only defines std::span when concepts
 // are also enabled. https://gcc.gnu.org/bugzilla/show_bug.cgi?id=97869
 #if defined(__cpp_lib_span) && __cpp_lib_span >= 202002L && \
diff --git a/include/range/v3/range_fwd.hpp b/range/v3/range_fwd.hpp
--- a/include/range/v3/range_fwd.hpp
+++ b/include/range/v3/range_fwd.hpp
@@ -1,3 +1,4 @@
+#include <string_view>
 /// \file
 // Range v3 library
 //
@@ -538,6 +539,12 @@
     template<typename R>
     RANGES_INLINE_VAR constexpr bool enable_borrowed_range = false;

+#if defined(__cpp_lib_string_view) && __cpp_lib_string_view >= 201603L
+    template<class CharT, class Traits>
+    RANGES_INLINE_VAR constexpr bool
+        enable_borrowed_range<std::basic_string_view<CharT, Traits>> = true;
+#endif
+
     namespace detail
     {
         template<typename R>
